# Mobile PWA design system

Light, calm, card-based UI (reference: Collabora Hub mockups). One accent color, generous whitespace, minimal buttons per screen.

## Layout & surfaces

- Page background: `#f3f6fb` (set in MobileShell) — never put color blocks directly on it.
- Content = stacked **white cards**: `rounded-3xl bg-white shadow-sm` with `px-4 py-3.5` padding. Page stack spacing `space-y-3`.
- Max 3–4 cards visible per screen; secondary actions collapse into text links, not more pill buttons.
- Hero (photo header) is compact: fixed height (~`h-28`), `rounded-3xl`, dark gradient overlay `from-slate-900/70`, white text.

## Color

- Single accent: **indigo-600** (`bg-indigo-600`, `text-indigo-600`). Hover `indigo-700`.
- Never mix two different accent blues in one screen (no `primary` + `indigo` side by side).
- Text: titles `text-slate-900 font-bold`, body `text-slate-500`, hints `text-slate-400`.
- Destructive: rose/red only for errors and overtime.

## Typography

- Card section label: `text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-400` (e.g. "SUIVI DU FORFAIT", "VOTRE ACCÈS").
- Key figures: `text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums` (+ `text-indigo-600` when accent).
- Hints/footnotes: `text-[11px] text-slate-500`.

## Buttons

- One **primary** filled button per screen max: `h-12 rounded-full bg-indigo-600 text-sm font-semibold`.
- Secondary: `variant="outline"` `h-11 rounded-full border-slate-200 text-slate-700` (or `border-indigo-200 text-indigo-700` when related to accent).
- Tertiary: plain text links `text-xs font-medium text-slate-500` with a small icon — never a third pill row.
- Café / Communauté / Événements / Profil live in the bottom nav — do not duplicate them as buttons on Accueil.

## Compactness (recurring feedback — apply by default)

The user has asked many times for blocks to take less space. Treat every new or edited block as compact-first:

- Status / summary blocks (counts, presence, points, promos, install nudges) are **one row**: `py-2.5`, icon or dot on the left, short text, optional small action on the right. Never a label line + big number line + separate hint row.
- Big figures (`text-2xl`) only for the page's single key metric (e.g. session timer). Counts inside a row use `text-sm font-bold tabular-nums`.
- Never render a zero state as a figure ("0 membre"). Replace it with a short phrase in the same row ("Personne sur place").
- Hints become a single `text-[11px]` phrase or a small inline link inside the row — no extra divider (`border-t`) section for one line of text.
- Optional controls (status toggles, composers) show only when relevant (e.g. member present) and sit inline in the same row when possible.
- Empty states: small card (`py-5`, icon `h-10 w-10`), one title + one hint line max.
- Avatar stacks: max 3–4 avatars at `h-7`, hide on very narrow screens if the row gets tight.
- Before adding a card, ask: can this be a row inside an existing card, a chip, or a toast instead?

## Progress & badges

- Progress bar: `h-2`–`h-2.5` rounded-full, indigo fill on `bg-slate-200`; caption row underneath (`text-[11px] text-slate-500`) with left/right labels (e.g. "Utilisé aujourd'hui" / "Expiration à minuit").
- Badges: soft tints (`bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-700`), rounded-md, small (`text-[10px]`).

## Patterns

- Announcement slot: `AnnouncementBanner` right under the hero — white card, sparkles icon in `bg-indigo-50` circle, one-line truncated text, dismissible (sessionStorage).
- Wi-Fi: circular glass button (`bg-white/20 backdrop-blur-sm`) in hero top-right; modal via `WifiCredentialsModal`.
- Scan QR stays the visually dominant action when the visitor has no session.
- Empty/pending states use a white card with centered slate text, never a bare `<Alert>` with default border.
- Engagement nudges (e.g. `CommunityNotePopup`) are transient toasts, not cards: floating above the bottom nav, auto-hide after ~6 s, dismissible, each item shown once (localStorage).

## React

- All hooks before any early `return` (Rules of Hooks — this page previously broke on `!ready` early return).
- Card components must render `null` cleanly when they have no data (e.g. no announcement, no Wi-Fi).
